-- statement:
--   **Residual of the segmented inverse** (exact Woodbury, all four stages perturbed).
--
--   The following holds (Lean statement, in the scope of module `Solutions.J6SegRes`):
--
--   ```lean
--   theorem J6Seg.res_bound (Mi : ℕ → ℕ → ℝ) {I J : Finset ℕ} {u W y y₂ x z : ℕ → ℝ}
--       {ε₁ ε₂ ε₃ ε₄ A d μ : ℝ} (hJI : J ⊆ I) (hblI : ∀ i ∈ I, bl i ⊆ I)
--       (hcl : ∀ i ∈ I, ∀ h ∈ Hs i, cl i h ∈ J)
--       (hMM : ∀ i ∈ I, ∀ f : ℕ → ℝ, Mv bl Mx (Mv bl Mi f) i = f i)
--       (hMi : ∀ (f : ℕ → ℝ) (F : ℝ), (∀ k ∈ I, |f k| ≤ F) → ∀ i ∈ I, |Mv bl Mi f i| ≤ μ * F)
--       (hA : ∀ i ∈ I, ∑ k ∈ bl i, |Mx i k| ≤ A) (hd : ∀ i ∈ I, ∑ h ∈ Hs i, |cf i h| ≤ d)
--       (hd0 : 0 ≤ d) (hμ : 0 ≤ μ) (hε₂ : 0 ≤ ε₂) (hε₃ : 0 ≤ ε₃) (hε₄ : 0 ≤ ε₄)
--       (hx : ∀ i, x i = y i - y₂ i)
--       (h1 : ∀ i ∈ I, |y i - Mv bl Mi u i| ≤ ε₁)
--       (h2 : ∀ i ∈ I, |y₂ i - Mv bl Mi W i| ≤ ε₂)
--       (h3 : ∀ i ∈ I, |W i - Dv Hs cl cf z i| ≤ ε₃)
--       (h4 : ∀ a ∈ J, |z a + Mv bl Mi (Dv Hs cl cf z) a - y a| ≤ ε₄) :
--       ∀ i ∈ I, |Mv bl Mx x i + Dv Hs cl cf x i - u i| ≤
--         A * (ε₁ + ε₂) + ε₃ + d * (ε₄ + μ * ε₃ + ε₂)
--   ```
--
--   **Context.** Segmented inverse (S2): the exact Woodbury residual identity (abstract form)
--
--   Abstract setting on positions `ℕ` (a position set `I`): a block-diagonal matrix `M` given by its
--   blocks `bl i` and entries `Mx`, its block inverse `Mi`, and a sparse coupling `Δ` given row-wise
--   by offsets `Hs i`, columns `cl i h` and coefficients `cf i h`, with every coupling column in the
--   capacitance index set `J`.
--
--   `res_bound` (report L8 + L10, residual form): if the four fixed-point stages of the segmented
--   inverse are accurate,
--   * `y ≈ M⁻¹ u` (`ε₁`), `W ≈ Δ z` (`ε₃`), `y₂ ≈ M⁻¹ W` (`ε₂`),
--   * `z + (M⁻¹ Δ z)|_J ≈ y|_J` (`ε₄`, the capacitance solve),
--
--   then `x = y - y₂` satisfies `|((M + Δ) x - u)_i| ≤ A(ε₁+ε₂) + ε₃ + d(ε₄ + μ ε₃ + ε₂)`
--   (`A`, `d`, `μ` bound `‖M‖`, `‖Δ‖`, `‖M⁻¹‖` row-wise). No exact intermediate solution is needed.
--   `Miv_bound`: `‖M⁻¹‖ ≤ 1/(1-m)` from `M M⁻¹ = I` and `‖M - I‖ ≤ m < 1` (via `near_id`).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** Part of the Lean formalization of the round-six κ-improvement (integer-multiplication-kappa campaign, target `IntMul.Kappa.jain_round6_framework`). The statement is copied verbatim from the Lean development; the platform node carries the same declaration name. Definitions it mentions live in the `IntMul_Kappa_R6_Defs*` bundles (on top of the published κ bundles `IntMul_Kappa_K_Defs*`).
